{
  "id": "chemotaxis-integral-adaptation-second-biology",
  "name": "Cooperative chemotaxis receptor methylation and perfect adaptation",
  "description": "Cooperative receptor activity feeds back onto methylation; the same equilibrium activity1/3 is recovered for different constant ligand inputs while methylation changes. Unbounded mean methylation is a local approximation, not an explicit finite-site receptor network or cell-motion model. Our illustrative linear F(a)=0.01*(1-a)-0.02*a specialization, team6,energy slope2,methylation reference1,ligand10,inactive/active affinities1/100,initialm1, time seconds,horizon500,RK4step0.1. Parameters are not an experimental fit. https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2551628/ Signed net-rate flows encode the stated differential equations. No clamps or resets. These educational equations are not fitted biological forecasts.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0807569105",
  "reference": "Tu, Shimizu and Berg (2008), Modeling the chemotactic response of Escherichia coli to time-varying stimuli, PNAS105:14855-14860, receptor-team free energy and activity-dependent methylation framework.",
  "category": "biology",
